  "prefLabel": "Saf-Mec 302.14 Applications by Out-of-State Licensees",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-Mec 302.14 Applications by Out-of-State Licensees. An out-of-state licensee seeking application for licensure shall be eligible for the licensing examination in plumbing and fuel gas fitting provided that he or she can demonstrate proof of licensure and/or certification from the state in which he or she are claiming to have worked, and provided further that the out-of-state licensee shall still comply with the prerequisites for the level of licensure sought regarding on-the-job experience, or its equivalent in an approved educational setting, as provided in RSA 153:27-38 and these rules.\n\nSource. #10847, eff 7-1-15 (from Saf-Mec 301.15)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-mec300.html"
